keywords:
  - "TRACE-FV"
  - "AI safety"
  - "conversational AI"
  - "black-box evaluation"
  - "epistemic calibration"
  - "trigger verification"
  - "correction endurance"
  - "reproducibility"
abstract: >-
  TRACE-FV is a black-box evaluation protocol for observable conversational-AI
  product behavior under frame variance, verified correction triggers, and
  correction endurance. This public Object A contains the scientific protocol,
  measurement framework, integrity requirements, scoring rubrics, disclosures,
  and related-work positioning. It contains no official pilot results.
